        "original_id": "beb04d41-c598-598d-9617-89d5e012c26d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Spreewerk, Walther\n- Products: Walther P.38, Luger P08, 8.8 cm Flak\n- Organizations: German Heer\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Before and during World War II, Spreewerk produced important weapons and components, including the 8.8 cm Flak anti-aircraft gun.\n- Before and during World War II, Spreewerk produced 280,880 Walther P.38 pistols.\n- The Walther P.38 was the standard service pistol of the German Heer.\n- The Walther P.38 was intended to replace the costly Luger P08.\n- Production of the Luger P08 was scheduled to end in 1942.",
